WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.300
Five analogies for how the model thinks.

00:00:00.889 --> 00:00:02.891
A cafe on a busy corner.

00:00:02.941 --> 00:00:06.617
A song stuck in your head.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.316
The fifth slice of pizza.

00:00:08.366 --> 00:00:09.719
Last year's star.

00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:11.818
And a flight simulator.

00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:14.346
The corner cafe sells coffee with no ads at all: that's baseline.

00:00:14.396 --> 00:00:21.691
Ads that keep working after they stop are adstock, like Slip, Slop, Slap.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.282
Each extra dollar adds less, like a fifth slice of pizza.

00:00:23.332 --> 00:00:28.730
A channel's average can hide what the next dollar does.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.102
So test the plan first.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.988
Use it like this:

00:00:33.038 --> 00:00:34.309
strip out baseline,

00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:35.417
credit carry-over,

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:36.632
find saturation,

00:00:36.682 --> 00:00:39.366
and test before committing budget.
